{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And the man called his wife's name Chavah.</b> By way of the plain sense (peshat): the word חוה means 'speaking,' from the root as in (Job 15) אחוך שמע לי; and this was from his great wisdom in the assigning of names. And he called her thus because he understood from her nature that she is talkative, and from here it is fitting that all women be talkative. And it says that she was 'the mother of all living' — that is, living of the speaking kind, to exclude other living creatures that do not possess intellect and speech." "<b>And by way of</b> the Midrash: 'his wife's name Chavah' is from the root חויא (serpent); and because he called her thus, the serpent was joined to her. From here our Rabbis of blessed memory learned: 'the name brings it about.'"], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:09:56.725421883Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}